      "unit_index": 1,
      "source_text": " 古歌：“世间情爱本飘摇，好似梦中渡雀桥。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "An old poem says: worldly love is by nature uncertain and drifting, like crossing the magpie bridge in a dream.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p02201",
      "unit_index": 2,
      "source_text": "渡过雀桥相见日，心头忧恨也难消。”",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Even on the day we cross the magpie bridge and meet, the sorrow and resentment in my heart are hard to dispel.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
